factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 7 problems
  The reel_script and slides say the three boys were 'missing' and 'lost' while playing; the article says they were reported missing (மாயம்) only as stated by reports, so the wording 'திடீரென மாயமானதாகக் கூறப்படுகிறது' is acceptable, but the slide 'ஞாயிற்றுக்கிழமை விளையாடச் சென்றபோது' is fine; however, the slide 'நீரில் மூழ்கி உயிரிழந்ததாக தகவல்' states a cause of death (drowning) that is in the article only as 'நீரில் மூழ்கி பரிதாபமாக உயிரிழந்த' in the closing summary — this is supported, so no problem there.
  The caption's '📰 முழு விவரம்' paragraph says the boys were 'மாயமானார்கள்' on Sunday and that parents searched 'தேடியும்' — supported. However the caption and reel_script say the bodies were found 'மிதந்தன' and that relatives found them ('உறவினர்கள் சடலங்களைக் கண்டனர்'), while the article says the relatives informed police after seeing the bodies — supported.
  Reel_script says the three boys are from 'நைனார்பாளையம் மற்றும் சின்னசேலம் பகுதியைச் சேர்ந்தவர்கள்' — the article says Imanuvel and Sham Abraham live in Nainarpalayam and Raja is from Chinnasalem, so this is supported.
  The slide 'யார் அவர்கள்?' bullet 'பெற்றோர் புகார் அளித்ததும் போலீசார் இரவு முழுவதும் தேடினர்' is placed under identity info but is a separate fact (police search), mixing two facts in one slide line.
  The slide and caption describe the boys as 'சடலமாக மீட்பு' and the caption says 'சடலங்கள் மிதந்தன' with the rescue by fire department — supported.
  The reel_script omits that the case is registered by Chinnasalem police only as a fact in the caption; the reel_script does mention 'வழக்குப் பதிவு செய்து' — present, no omission.
  The caption's English line 'Chinnasalem lake 3 boys dead, police probe | Salem news' is an English addition not in the article's Tamil text, though the article's English subtitle 'Sensation in Chinnasalem: Bodies of 3 boys recovered from a lake' supports the content.
